course: dictionary
lesson: 8857
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Shoot is a word with many meanings, so the sentence tells you which one to use. Read the words around it and ask: what is happening here? In «Some seeds are shot out when the pod bursts open», something is being sent flying out fast, so shoot means to be thrown or flung out.
explain: «The car shot past.» A car cannot fire a gun here, so shoot must mean to move very fast. Test your meaning: "The car moved very fast past" still makes sense, so you have the right one.
explain: Shoot can also be a noun. In science, a shoot is the first green growth from a seed, and roots go down while shoots go up. When you meet shoot, check the clues first, then try the meaning you think fits.
fact: Shoot can be a verb (shoot, shoots, shot, shooting) or a noun (a shoot, shoots).
fact: «Shoot» can mean to fire a gun or arrow, or to kick or throw a ball at the goal in sport.
fact: «Shoot» can mean to move very fast, or to make a film or photo with a camera.
fact: A shoot is a new young part growing from a plant, and roots go down while shoots go up.
fact: «Shoot!» is a mild word said when something goes wrong, instead of a swear word.
exercise: «Some seeds are shot out when the pod bursts open, like peas.» What does shot out mean here? | Eaten by birds | Planted in a pot | Painted bright green | *Flung out fast
exercise: In football, what does «shoot at goal» mean? | To sit on the bench and watch | *To kick or throw the ball at the goal | To run around the pitch slowly | To hold the ball and stand still
exercise: «The gardener spotted a new shoot growing from the bean seed.» Find and copy the word that means a new young part of a plant. | spotted | seed | gardener | *shoot
test: «Beans shoot up quickly in warm sunshine.» What does shoot up mean? | Fall down into the soil | *Grow fast or rise quickly | Sing loudly | Turn brown and stop growing
test: Jayden drops his lunch and says, «Shoot!» What does this show? | A rude word he must never use | A word for a camera | *A mild word said when something goes wrong, not a swear word | A sign he is going to fire a gun
exam: «The team had a photo shoot in the park.» What does photo shoot mean here? | *A session of taking photos with a camera | A quick fight with a gun | A game where players kick a ball at goal | A race to see who can grow fastest
